    {
      "type": "code",
      "chapter": "The limiter",
      "narration": "The limiter buckets each IP into a one-minute window, increments a Redis counter, and sets the expiry only on the first hit. Past twenty requests it answers 429 with a Retry-After header.",
      "hunkId": "h2",
      "focusLinesAfter": [
        "11-18"
      ],
      "calloutText": "Expiry is set once per window, so the key cleans itself up."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "chapter": "Wiring it in",
      "narration": "The server mounts the limiter on the orders route and publishes an event after the order is saved.",
      "hunkId": "h3",
      "focusLinesAfter": [
        8,
        12
      ],
      "calloutText": "publish runs after the insert, so a queue outage fails the request.",
      "view": "morph"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "chapter": "Real prices",
      "narration": "Order totals used a hard-coded price of ten. They now look up each SKU in parallel, and empty orders are rejected up front.",
      "hunkId": "h6",
      "calloutText": "Pricing lookups run in parallel with Promise.all."
    },
    {
      "type": "er",
      "chapter": "Data model",
      "title": "orders",
      "narration": "The orders table gains a status column, starting as pending. Totals are now computed from the pricing service, and each order still belongs to one user with many line items.",
